diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 5716767..654ea8a 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -5,5 +5,8 @@ Imports the booking batches that the branch offices upload into the ledger table
 - `api/upload.py` writes each upload to `/srv/ledger/inbox`.
 - `ledger/scheduler.py` runs `WORKERS` import processes. Each one claims an inbox file by renaming it and calls `import_file()`.
 - A rejected file goes to `/srv/ledger/rejected`. Any other failure puts the file back into the inbox for the next round.
+- An imported file goes to `/srv/ledger/archive/<day>/<batch>.csv`, the audit copy. docs/batch-format.md describes the format and the archive rule.
 
 The branch offices pick the batch names. Two offices can upload a batch of the same name at the same time.
+
+Each import holds the ledger advisory lock while it writes, like the API. It waits at most `LEDGER_LOCK_TIMEOUT` for it.
diff --git a/docs/batch-format.md b/docs/batch-format.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..cf06fd7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/batch-format.md
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+# Batch file format, version 2
+
+A batch file is UTF-8 CSV with a header line:
+
+```
+#batch=<name> rows=<count> currency=<code>
+<account>,<amount>,<booked on>
+...
+```
+
+- `name`: 1 to 40 characters from `A-Z a-z 0-9 _ -`. The office picks it.
+- `count`: the number of booking lines. At most 50 000.
+- `code`: EUR, USD, GBP, or CHF. Each currency has its own ledger table.
+- `amount`: a decimal number with a point, such as `-12.50`.
+- `booked on`: an ISO date.
+
+## Import
+
+The importer refuses a file whose line count differs from the header, so a partial upload never reaches the ledger.
+
+After the import, the file moves to `archive/<YYYY-MM-DD>/<name>.csv`. The archive is the audit copy: a second batch of the same name on the same day is rejected and never replaces it. The office must upload it under a new name.
+
+Version 1 files (no header, EUR only) are refused from this release on. All offices send version 2 since March.
